turnip: no BV pipe on the Adreno 722

The A722 has no BV pipe for concurrent binning (the downstream driver
treats gen7_17_0 as a no-CB part). Registering the BV bin preamble on it
leaves the context without the BR one: after an L1 preemption with
skipsaverestore the context resumed with the CCU still in the other
context's mode, and GMEM writes went to system memory at their GMEM
offsets, CCU write faults at iova 0x0-0x1240 and corrupted tiles.

Add a has_bv property, set for every a7xx and a8xx except the A722, and use
it for the BV bin preamble and for concurrent binning.

--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
@@ -113,6 +113,9 @@ struct fd_dev_info {
 
       /* info for setting RB_CCU_CNTL */
       bool concurrent_resolve;
+
+      /* Whether the CP has the BV pipe used for concurrent binning (a7xx+). */
+      bool has_bv;
       bool has_z24uint_s8uint;
 
       /* on a650, vertex shader <-> tess control io uses LDL/STL */
